{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787032780,"nonce":"qRC16pc7reZBn9iTTtoDAllbOsE=","message":"Done in a5786e4. ADR 0036 written first, as §A.1 required.\n\nalerts.Occurrence → alerts.Case and alert_occurrences → alert_cases: ~230 Go identifiers over 228 files, 1 table, 7 columns, 27 constraints, 10 indexes, 4 routes, 8 event types, 41 TS/TSX files, client regenerated.\n\nPersisted history is CANONICALISED, not rewritten. alert_events is monthly-partitioned, append-only, 13-month retention, so a bulk UPDATE is a table-doubling deploy outage that still cannot reach cold partitions. NewEventType folds the eight occurrence.* spellings onto their case.* value; SQL predicates spell both via PersistedSpellings(). Small bounded tables ARE rewritten: alert_event_keys, enrichments, ui_events, delivery_drills.failed_stage, and river_job.kind plus args.occurrence_id — that last one is a persisted DTO the ticket never mentions, and missing it would have failed every in-flight enrich.run.\n\nTHE WIRE IS NOT RENAMED. The rename had reached internal/channels/render/webhookjson/envelope.go, emitting case and total_cases under an unchanged oto.notification.v1 — which SPEC §H.10 and SCOPE-BOUNDARY H-2 forbid, and which this same branch refuses to do elsewhere (it keeps alert_groups.receiver precisely because it is on this envelope). Reverted to occurrence/total_occurrences with the Go names left as Case, and frozen by new golden fixtures. occurrence is not a §A.1 banned word, so the wire spelling was a preference, not doctrine.\n\nThree errors in the ticket, verified: there are EIGHT EventOccurrence* constants at event.go:66-80, not ten; there is no Go identifier AlertOccurrence (it is alerts.Occurrence at occurrence.go:24); and idempotency.go needs NO change — :19 is SubjectAlertGroup, SubjectKind is at :16, and notifications_subjkind_ck admits only alert_group, so nothing occurrence-flavoured exists there. The SPEC citation is :89, not :90.","files":null}]}